.TH CSTRING_RESERVE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cstring_reserve \- pre-allocate capacity for at least min_capacity bytes
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cstring.h>

bool cstring_reserve(cstr s, size_t min_capacity);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Makes sure that the internal buffer has room for min_capacity bytes or
more. That count includes the null terminator. The function rounds the
requested size up to the nearest power of two (minimum 16). It does
nothing when the current capacity is already large enough.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s              String to change
min_capacity   Minimum number of bytes to reserve (including null terminator)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
true on success, and also when the capacity was already large enough
false when the reallocation fails, or when the requested size is too
large
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Asserts if s is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_create_full (3)
